{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">- Unary negative operator</span>\n","class":"manual","created":2879,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310867","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Unary-negative-operator.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Unary-negative-operator.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">- Unary negative operator</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Reverses the sign of a numeric expression.\nDo not confuse this operator with the subtraction operator that\nsubtracts one expression from another.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator__syntax_GC152A2679097\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d269618e103\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator__idGDE1V92661738\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>- <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression whose value is numeric.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator__example_GC152B2679103\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d269618e146\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">If\nyou supply a negative value for the variable <code class=\"ph codeph\">fx</code>,\nthe <span class=\"ph filepath\">r-uneg.p</span> procedure uses the unary negative\noperator (-) to reverse the sign of <code class=\"ph codeph\">fx</code>, producing\nthe absolute value of <code class=\"ph codeph\">fx</code> (<code class=\"ph codeph\">fabs-x</code>).</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-uneg.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator__idGDE1VA2661743\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE fx     AS DECIMAL NO-UNDO LABEL &quot;X&quot;.\nDEFINE VARIABLE fabs-x AS DECIMAL NO-UNDO LABEL &quot;ABS(X)&quot;.\n\nREPEAT:\n  SET fx.\n  IF fx &lt; 0 THEN\n   <strong class=\"ph b\">fabs-x = -fx.</strong>\n  ELSE \n    fabs-x = fx.\n  DISPLAY fabs-x.\nEND.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-negative-operator__see-also_GC152C2679115\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d269618e199\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Unary-positive-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Unary-positive-operator.html\">+ Unary positive operator</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Datetime-addition-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Datetime-addition-operator.html\">+ Datetime addition operator</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Subtraction-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Subtraction-operator.html\">- Subtraction operator</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310867","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":2879,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"- Unary negative operator","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Unary-negative-operator.html","type":"Manual"}